---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Technical Writing & Architecture Notes — Pedro Ivo Vasconcelos" description="Technical executive summaries, architectural deep dives, and performance case studies by Pedro Ivo Vasconcelos on data platforms, query tuning, and applied AI.">
  <main id="conteudo" class="container" style="padding-top: 3rem; padding-bottom: 5rem;">
    <div class="section-heading" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Engineering Insights · Architecture Summaries</p>
      <h1>Technical Writing & Architecture Notes</h1>
      <p>
        Deep dives into real-world database optimization, cloud warehouse storage efficiency, deterministic modeling, and agentic systems.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); margin-bottom: 3rem; max-width: 52rem;">
      <strong style="color: var(--text); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">
        📌 Architecture Summaries & Technical Briefs · Resumos Técnicos de Arquitetura
      </strong>
      <p style="color: var(--text-soft); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;">
        The entries below are concise executive summaries and architectural findings derived from verified production benchmarks and software systems. Complete long-form research papers and empirical datasets will be published as dedicated standalone articles as each peer-review cycle is finalized.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2.5rem; max-width: 52rem;">
      <!-- Article 1: Snowflake Cost & Storage -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent); margin: 0;">Cloud Data Warehousing · Cost Optimization</span>
          <span class="tag" style="background: var(--surface-soft); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.75rem;">Executive Summary / Resumo</span>
        </div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--text);">
          How We Cut Snowflake Cloud Storage by ~60% Through Clustering and Lifecycle Optimization
        </h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          An empirical breakdown of storage bloat in analytical warehouses. Covers how redundant transient micro-partitions, unoptimized Time Travel retention windows, and missing clustering keys inflated monthly bills, and the exact governance strategy used to reclaim ~60% of cloud storage capacity at CI&T.
        </p>
        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-soft);">
          <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Auditing table fail-safe retention, converting staging tables to transient, and clustering by query prune paths yield immediate compound cost reductions without impacting query latency.
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Article 2: PostgreSQL Performance -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent); margin: 0;">Database Performance · Query Tuning</span>
          <span class="tag" style="background: var(--surface-soft); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.75rem;">Executive Summary / Resumo</span>
        </div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--text);">
          Bringing PostgreSQL p95 Query Latency Down to ~30ms: Indexing & Partitioning Realities
        </h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Investigating slow sequential scans and index bloat on high-write relational tables. Examines `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` execution plans, partial composite index design, table range partitioning, and autovacuum tuning that brought 95th-percentile query response times from multi-second spikes down to ~30 milliseconds.
        </p>
        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-soft);">
          <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Indexes that match predicate selectivity rather than full-column coverage drastically shrink buffer cache footprint and eliminate sequential disk reads.
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Article 3: Deterministic Simulation -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent); margin: 0;">Simulation · Systems Engineering</span>
          <span class="tag" style="background: var(--surface-soft); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.75rem;">Executive Summary / Resumo</span>
        </div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--text);">
          Deterministic Orbital Mechanics in Pure Python: Lessons from CCT World Engine
        </h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Building an orbital and seasonal simulation engine without floating-point drift across platforms. Details the implementation of Keplerian barycentric physics, multi-calendar synchronization, and pytest validation suites verifying astronomical ephemeris across millennial simulation scales.
        </p>
        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-soft);">
          <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Determinism is achieved by fixing time step discretizations and isolating transcendental float approximations into normalized unit intervals.
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Article 4: WebGL Games & PostMessage SDK -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent); margin: 0;">Computer Graphics · Web Architecture</span>
          <span class="tag" style="background: var(--surface-soft); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.75rem;">Executive Summary / Resumo</span>
        </div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--text);">
          Building Zero-Friction WebGL 3D Games with Babylon.js and Isolated SDK Sandboxes
        </h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          How Work & Slop Games delivers 11 browser-native 3D arcade games with zero layout friction. Highlights include 100dvh full-bleed canvas rendering, auto-hiding navigation bars, WebGL context loss recovery, and a strict postMessage isolation boundary that prevents game runtimes from leaking state to the host application.
        </p>
        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-soft);">
          <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Treating interactive canvas viewports as self-contained micro-applications with explicit message contracts eliminates DOM interference and ensures rock-solid 60 FPS performance.
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Article 5: Model Context Protocol (MCP) -->
      <article class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--accent); margin: 0;">Applied AI · Agentic Protocols</span>
          <span class="tag" style="background: var(--surface-soft); color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.75rem;">Executive Summary / Resumo</span>
        </div>
        <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 0.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; color: var(--text);">
          Model Context Protocol (MCP) in Production: Bridging Agentic LLMs to Live Developer Toolchains
        </h2>
        <p style="color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          Moving beyond brittle custom function calling. Examines how the Model Context Protocol standardizes agent interaction with databases, Git repositories, and cloud control planes while enforcing fail-closed security gates, audit trails, and zero unauthorized state mutations.
        </p>
        <div style="background: var(--surface-soft); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-soft);">
          <strong>Key Takeaway:</strong> Autonomous agents require protocol-level authorization boundaries and immutable audit logs before they can be safely trusted in production environments.
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
